    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d750">

                <pb facs="0960" n="950" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg950"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3–947: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-10T18:00:00-05:00">March 10, 1947—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>292. Copy of minutes of conference held Feb 20 between SecWar [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">SecState</hi>] and SecNavy forwarded air pouch Feb
                        28<anchor n="21" xml:id="d750-f1"/> (Embtel 493 Mar 9).</p>
                <p>Following is summary of pertinent decisions reached at conference: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>NAG should carry out full program specified Public Law 512. SecState
                            raised no objection to separate agreement for NAG but pointed out
                            decision should be reached only after consultation with War.</item>
                        <pb facs="0961" n="951" xml:id="pg951"/>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>No further transfers should be made through Lend-Lease
                            procedures.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>SecState assented to issuance at this time of executive order
                            implementing PL 512 (copy of draft executive order which has received
                            informal approval by State and Navy being forwarded air pouch).</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>On recommendation SecState, SecNavy concurred in reduction of Marines
                            in China to 3,500 subject to review in 6 mos with view to further
                            downward revision.</item>
                        <label>5.</label>
                        <item>SecState indicated it was for Navy to decide whether flag officer
                            should relieve present Naval Attaché Nanking.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
